From 0cebbaf82bdc21a63fbf711230d46a043ba9a2bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 08:57:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] transports: tenant_providers response shapes + PUT key +
 full key payload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cluster of follow-up fixes the first real UI exercise of the
multi-tenant admin surface forced into the open. All landed in one
patch because they're variations of the same underlying mistake:
the v1 tenant-scoped handlers were returning slim {tenant_id,
provider, ...} envelopes that didn't match the rich shapes the UI's
RTK Query mutations + optimistic cache updates expect.

Behavioral fixes (each one a real "doesn't work" report from
browser testing):

  1. POST /api/tenants/{tid}/providers used to return
     {tenant_id, provider}. The UI's createProvider mutation does
     draft.push(newProvider) then sortProviders which reads .name —
     undefined .name throws inside .localeCompare and the React
     error boundary surfaces "Something went wrong". Now returns
     the full ProviderResponse shape (name, network_config,
     concurrency_and_buffer_size, provider_status, …) via a new
     buildTenantProviderResponse helper that mirrors the legacy
     ProviderHandler.getProviderResponseFromConfig without taking
     a *ProviderHandler receiver.

  2. GET /api/tenants/{tid}/providers returned providers as a
     MAP keyed by name; the UI expects an ARRAY of rows each with
     .name. The map-keyed response flattened into a list of empty
     ModelProvider objects and the providers list rendered zero
     rows even when the tenant had providers. Now returns
     {providers: [...], total} matching ListProvidersResponse.

  3. GET /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{p} returned
     {tenant_id, provider, config: {...}}; the UI expects the rich
     shape at the top level. Same fix.

  4. PUT /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{p} (update) returned the
     same slim shape — same React error boundary on save. Same fix.

  5. POST /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{p}/keys was reading just
     {ID, Name, Value} and silently dropping Models, Weight,
     Enabled, Aliases, BlacklistedModels, and every key-type-
     specific config. So the UI's add-key form let the user pick
     models but they never persisted; inference 400'd with "no
     keys found that support model: X". Payload now embeds the
     full schemas.Key; Models defaults to ["*"] when omitted (the
     legacy single-tenant flow's behaviour).

  6. PUT /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{p}/keys/{key_id} (key
     update) was MISSING ENTIRELY — fasthttp's MethodNotAllowed
     returned a 4xx and the UI's edit-key form silently failed.
     New handler takes the full schemas.Key, ID pinned from URL
     (NOT body) so a typo'd id can't redirect the update,
     carries forward Name/Value/Models when the body left them
     blank, redacts Value in the response, evicts the per-tenant
     runtime.

Tests:
  - tenant_providers_test.go updated to assert the new array-shape
    list response. Old map-shape would have masked future regressions.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
